RULER of_record=tools/ulp_policy.py format=f32 bits=32 mant=23 exp=8 bias=127 sign=0x80000000
POPULATION pairs=290297 clean=289168 nan=1129 straddling=5612 signed_zero=2 involving_inf=12 derived_from=every_bf16_image(widened) x {+-1,flip,binade} + f32 exponents x mants x {flip,+-1,+-2}
CHECK name=the pair population contains every class the repair is about ok=1 n=290297 a population with no straddling pair could not show the old body's complement law at all, and one with no NaN could not show the refusal
CHECK name=the repaired ulpdist equals the shared ruler on every pair it counts ok=1 n=289168 289168 finite-and-infinite pairs compared against Ruler.classify; first disagreement: None
CHECK name=the repaired ulpdist REFUSES exactly the pairs the ruler answers None for ok=1 n=400 400 NaN-involving pairs asked one at a time, all raised (a sentinel here would widen a band with a number that means nothing); pairs it counted anyway: none
LAW old = 2^32+1-d on straddling pairs: holds on 5610 of 5610 (of which the signed-zero pair class accounts for 2 of 2); old == d on 283556 same-sign pairs, violations 0
HEADLINE pair=+0/-0                    ruler=1 historic=4294967296 repaired=1 repaired_matches_ruler=1
CHECK name=the repaired ruler states +0/-0 the way the ruler of record does ok=1 n=1 historic body said 4294967296 where tools/ulp_policy.py says 1 — this is the pair class the bands were blind to
